Sure! To update a `break` node’s label to `"loopEnd"` only when it isn’t already set to that value, you’ll need to pass the node (as a stringified JavaScript object) and the desired label to the `updateBreak` function.

Here’s a quick example of how you’d call it:

```javascript
const node = /* your break node as a JSON string */;
const result = updateBreak({
  node: node,
  label: "loopEnd"
});
```

If you can share the exact JSON representation of the break node you’re working with, I can show you the exact call and the resulting updated node.
